command-list: configure the commands tpm-rs does not implement as CC_NO

Classification: profile setting.

The implemented command set is a profile choice. Commands that tpm-rs does
not implement (tpm2-impl engine.rs SUPPORTED_COMMANDS) are configured CC_NO
so that both TPMs expose the same command set (TPM_CAP_COMMANDS,
TPM_PT_TOTAL_COMMANDS, TPM_PT_LIBRARY_COMMANDS) and reject the same command
codes with TPM_RC_COMMAND_CODE. TPM2_CertifyX509 and the vendor commands are
disabled by profile-no-certify-x509.patch and profile-no-vendor-commands.patch.

Commands configured CC_NO here: ACT_SetTimeout, ECC_Decrypt, ECC_Encrypt,
EC_Ephemeral, PP_Commands, PolicyCapability, PolicyParameters,
PolicyPhysicalPresence, SetAlgorithmSet, ZGen_2Phase, NV_DefineSpace2,
NV_ReadPublic2. Commands that tpm-rs implements but the reference does not:
none (so no harness exception is needed); the TPM2_HMAC/TPM2_HMAC_Start and
TPM2_MAC/TPM2_MAC_Start variants share their command codes.

diff --git a/src/TpmProfile_CommandList.h b/src/TpmProfile_CommandList.h
